These numbers are computed from this binder's own real facts via SPARQL —
not hand-maintained, not estimated.

## The binder

| # | Document | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| 01 | `01-SYSTEM-DESCRIPTION.md` | The audited system's real boundaries and components |
| 02 | `02-MANAGEMENT-ASSERTION.md` | The company's own draft assertion — not generated content, a place for a real person to write one |
| 03 | `03-CONTROL-MATRIX.md` | Every one of the 28 TSC criteria, one row each, status visible whether addressed or not |
| 04 | `04-EVIDENCE-INVENTORY.md` | The flat evidence list backing the matrix |
| 05 | `05-AUDITOR-TEST-MATRIX.md` | The CPA firm's side: rehearsed test procedures and results, mirroring a real report's Section 4 |
| 06 | `06-ENGAGEMENT-TIMELINE.md` | All 10 audit-engagement phases, in order, status visible whether started or not |
| 07 | `07-EXCEPTION-LOG.md` | Every finding, its risk level, its remediation status |
| 08 | `08-SUBSERVICE-ORGANIZATIONS.md` | Vendors/subprocessors this system's scope depends on, and CUECs |

## The one thing this binder cannot do

Issue an opinion. That is the one section of a real SOC 2 Type II report —
the Independent Service Auditor's Report — that requires an actual
licensed CPA firm, after an actual independent audit engagement. Every
document above exists to make that engagement, when it happens, start from
real evidence instead of a blank page — not to make the engagement
unnecessary.
